how do you use a color palette is there  a rule as to how much of each color to  use there is a rule in fact but rules  are also meant to be broken but let's  start with the rule so here I'll show  you 60 30 10 they equal 100% so  essentially this is kind of like the  baseline color ratio that I would  probably start with so the 60 percent is  obviously the color that will be used  the most 60 would be like your primary  color so this is like your hero the 30%  is your secondary color it's used about  half as much but you know it's still  fairly visible and then the 10% that's  the accent color that's that's kind of  like your little wild card where you see  this work really well is in web design  so maybe your background could be the  secondary color if you want it light  right this kind of life right here and  then maybe your headers are blue or  something right and then where you might  use your accent color this little 10% is  maybe in calls to action so like on a  button or on something that pops up like  things that you really want to get  people's attention and you want them to  look at that's where you would use that  that little 10% yeah accent color a lot  of times you'll have kind of different  types of the same color and I like to  keep them in in the same kind of ratio  so let's say you have like I like blue  with dark blue you know there's like  it's kind of really light color then  there's like a brown or a tan then you  have a couple different shades of the  accent color just to kind of expand the  palette a bit  I still like to keep them grouped by  ratio so I sort of put all the cool  colors over here in the blue and then  even though this is kind of creamy it's  it's like it's still warm  so I pair it round together and then a  few the two purples are the accent over  here so that's a very quick baseline for  just taking all your colors and trying  to like try to basically just ration  them in a way that that makes sense if  you enjoyed this video then you're  really going to like my  course that's right I teach a course  it's called color for creatives then we  go over color theory how to pair colors  together and I'll walk you through my  whole process for building palettes and  then using it in my illustration work  it's pretty neat  visit the futurecom slash color and  learn more about it  [Music]
 

